ot?</li>
<li>=F0=9F=A4=94 Why do I sometimes get an infinite refetching loop?</li>
<li>=F0=9F=A4=94 Why do I sometimes get an old state or prop value inside m=
y effect?</li>
</ul>
<p>When I just started using Hooks, I was confused by all of those question=
s too. Even when writing the initial docs, I didn=E2=80=99t have a firm gra=
sp on some of the subtleties. I=E2=80=99ve since had a few =E2=80=9Caha=E2=
=80=9D moments that I want to share with you. <strong>This deep dive will m=
ake the answers to these questions look obvious to you.</strong></p>
<p>To <em>see</em> the answers, we need to take a step back. The goal of th=
is article isn=E2=80=99t to give you a list of bullet point recipes. It=E2=
=80=99s to help you truly =E2=80=9Cgrok=E2=80=9D <code>useEffect</code>. Th=
ere won=E2=80=99t be much to learn. In fact, we=E2=80=99ll spend most of ou=
r time <em>un</em>learning.</p>
<p><strong>It=E2=80=99s only after I stopped looking at the <code>useEffect=
</code> Hook through the prism of the familiar class lifecycle methods that=
 everything came together for me.</strong></p>
