//wsvincent.com/javascript-closure-settimeout-for-loop/">the canonical wron=
g-value-in-a-timeout confusion</a> that=E2=80=99s often associated with clo=
sures. This is because the actual source of the confusion in this example i=
s the mutation (React mutates <code>this.state</code> in classes to point t=
o the latest state) and not closures themselves.</p>
<p><strong>Closures are great when the values you close over never change. =
That makes them easy to think about because you=E2=80=99re essentially refe=
rring to constants.</strong> And as we discussed, props and state never cha=
nge within a particular render. By the way, we can fix the class version=E2=
=80=A6 by <a target=3D"_blank" class=3D" scale-100 active:scale-100" style=
