/a>.</p>
<p>Be aware that when you want to read the <em>future</em> props or state f=
rom a function in a <em>past</em> render, you=E2=80=99re swimming against t=
he tide. It=E2=80=99s not <em>wrong</em> (and in some cases necessary) but =
it might look less =E2=80=9Cclean=E2=80=9D to break out of the paradigm. Th=
is is an intentional consequence because it helps highlight which code is f=
ragile and depends on timing. In classes, it=E2=80=99s less obvious when th=
is happens.</p>
