there if our code needs them.</p>
<h2>Synchronization, Not Lifecycle</h2>
<p>One of my favorite things about React is that it unifies describing the =
initial render result and the updates. This <a target=3D"_blank" class=3D" =
scale-100 active:scale-100" style=3D"opacity:1;transition:transform 0.2s ea=
se-in-out, opacity 0.2s 0.4s linear" href=3D"https://overreacted.io/the-bug=
-o-notation/">reduces the entropy</a> of your program.</p>
<p>Say my component looks like this:</p>
